course: dictionary
lesson: 945
title: Describing hair with blond
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words tell you what something looks like. «Blond» is one of them: it tells the reader what colour someone's hair is. «She had long blond hair that shone in the sun.» Blond means pale yellow or golden.
explain: Use the words around it to check. Hair, shone and sun are clues that point to a light, golden colour. Then try a swap: «She had long pale yellow hair that shone in the sun» still makes sense, so your meaning fits.
explain: Blond can also describe colour in things that are not people. «The table was made of blond wood» means the wood is pale and golden. Blond can be a noun too: «The blond waved from the boat» means a person with blond hair.
fact: Blond means having pale yellow or golden hair.
fact: Blond can also describe colour, such as «blond wood», which is pale golden wood.
fact: A blond is a person with blond hair. Blonde, with an e, is often used for women.
fact: «Strawberry blonde» means reddish blond, and «platinum blonde» means very pale blond.
fact: In French, «brun» means dark-haired, «blond» means blond, and «roux» means ginger.
exercise: «Her hair was blond and curly, like golden sunshine.» What does blond mean? | Dark brown | *Pale yellow or golden | Silver grey | Bright red
exercise: «The blond wood of the new table shone in the light.» What does blond describe here? | *The colour of the wood | The table's age | The price | The size of the table
exercise: Find and copy the word that tells the colour of hair: «The blonde girl waved from the boat.» | waved | girl | boat | *blonde
test: «Mia's brother has strawberry blonde hair.» What does strawberry blonde mean? | Very pale, almost white | *Reddish blond | Curly and wet | Dark brown
test: Which word means a person with blond hair? | *A blond | Blonding | Blondly | Blondness
exam: In French, «brun» means dark-haired and «blond» means blond. Which French word means ginger? | brun | blond | *roux | rouge
